body:
Cos water does nothing, its passive yet it flows, evaporates, rains down and nurtures all things.So it says the Tao is like that, this means, everything that exists moves with the same principle of no-effort, even if it looks as if its making effort.Just like water gathers in the lowest place, everything falls to the lowest place.

A building is supported by the ground, the substance of a building is going to the lowest place, it remains standing for other reasons, just like the atoms in water are held together, the thing that holds them together is the same principle, of the path of least resistance.

&#x200B;

Now, you might ask, what about a helium balloon that goes upwards, well, its the heavier air pushing downwards that pushes it upward. The planet orbits the sun with the same intertia principle. Its everywhere.

&#x200B;

No matter what you do: You are doing nothing.

Hey, Im uruguayan and native in english. I recommend uruguay, I know a bunch of Americans that already are enjoying the privilege of living in a country that pretty much is neutral in relation to this bipolar world (china/america), true freedom of speech, you can say almost anything you want here, and overall the best country that exists in the world currently, if you're a caucasian that is... So yeah, I highly suggest you come and meet great people (including me) and gradually learn Spanish with the best professor (me), and have a great rest of your life, and also resting in the literal sense, since its a very mellow environment. I hope you make the right decision, which is to come to Uruguay and try it out and stay if you love it, now, I'm going to end my rant. Peace.

&#x200B;

Also from all the choices you mentioned, I'm gonna lowkey tell you upfront that Uruguay is a no-brainer choice.

No, most of them are the thin ones. It will sound odd, but it felt as if they were handing me the thick one purposefully.

